-- title:
--   Ogg's element at a crossing point: tt'=q¹²
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0\ge 1$ and a prime $q$ with $q\nmid N_0$, and let $\mathfrak X$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package `DRModelPackageLevel N₀ q hqN` for level $\Gamma_0(N_0q)$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain, $\rho_O \colon$ `DRLevel.R q` $\to O$ a ring homomorphism, and assume the maximal ideal of $O$ is generated by the image of $q$, i.e. $\mathfrak m_O = (q)$. Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$ and $\mathrm{to}\kappa \colon O \to \kappa$ a ring homomorphism. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two morphisms `𝔛.comp κ (toκ.comp ρO) 0` and `𝔛.comp κ (toκ.comp ρO) 1` (the two branches of the geometric fibre at $\kappa$), and let $x_n =$ `𝔛.crossingPt ρO toκ n` be its image in `DRLevel.XO ρO`, the base change of the model to $O$, namely the image of $n$ under the first projection followed by `𝔛.comp κ (toκ.comp ρO) 0` followed by `DRLevel.bcMap ρO toκ`. Assume both points `𝔛.ξinf ρO toκ` and `𝔛.ξzero ρO toκ` specialise to $x_n$, with specialisation witnesses `hinf` and `hzero`. Then there exist $t, t'$ in the local ring of `DRLevel.XO ρO` at $x_n$ such that $t\,t'$ equals the twelfth power of `baseGerm ρO x_n ((q : ℕ) : O)`, the germ at $x_n$ of the global section pulled back from $q \in O$ along the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} O$; moreover $t$ lies in the maximal ideal of that local ring, and the image of $t$ under at least one of the two specialisation maps (to the stalk at `𝔛.ξinf ρO toκ`, or to the stalk at `𝔛.ξzero ρO toκ`) is a unit.
--
--   This is the local equation of the two crossing branches of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(N_0q)$ over $O$ at a supersingular crossing point, with $t$ the germ of Ogg's modular unit $\Delta(\tau)/\Delta(q\tau)$ or of its partner $q^{12}$ divided by it, each of which is invertible on exactly one of the two branches. It is used by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.forall_exists_orientedCrossingChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.forall_exists_orientedCrossingChart) to produce oriented local charts at the crossings.
